  "chromebook_touch_a11y_notes": [
   "Many school Chromebooks are low-end (Celeron/MediaTek, 4GB RAM): keep SVG filter count low (one shared feDropShadow), avoid animating filters; animate transform/opacity only.",
   "Touch: set touch-action:none on draggable SVG elements, use setPointerCapture, hit targets >=44px (enlarge with transparent stroke on clock hands).",
   "Stylus Chromebooks expose PointerEvent.pressure for perfect-freehand.",
   "Rotation drag: angle = atan2(dy,dx) relative to center via getScreenCTM(); snap minute hand 6deg, hour hand linked (0.5deg/min).",
   "A11y: each draggable must also be operable by keyboard (Radix Slider or role=slider with aria-valuenow/aria-valuetext e.g. '3시 30분'); provide <title>/<desc> in SVG; respect prefers-reduced-motion.",
   "Audio (Tone.js/abcjs) must start from a user gesture.",
   "Managed Chromebooks may block some CDNs via admin policy - self-host vendored copies as fallback; GSAP license allows bundling.",
   "Korean fonts: subset/woff2 to keep offline-ish performance; print uses same font."
  ]
